[verdict]
  final task-0 MSE: baseline 2.26 | oracle 0.097 | router-naive 2.20 | router-super 1.745  (chance 1.50)
  - router-NAIVE collapses to 1/6 slots -> reverts to the baseline (2.20, 23x oracle): unsupervised context DISCOVERY is the hard part, not θ=f(c) generation.
  - router-SUPERVISED (task-label routing, trained ONLINE alongside the head) roughly halves the forgetting (1.74 vs baseline 2.26) but stays 18x the oracle and its OWN slots drift to 3/6 distinct with task-0 confidence falling off -> THE ROUTER IS ITSELF A SEQUENTIAL LEARNER THAT FORGETS.
  Actionable: the θ=f(c) generation is not the bottleneck — context INFERENCE is. Use an OFFLINE-pretrained router over all contexts (H-C4's domain_head.pt is exactly that: trained once on 88 domains, not online), or harden the router too. An online-learned router recreates the very forgetting problem H0 solves for the head.
